g sure the error handling follows existing patterns and gets proper differential test coverage against the GNU version. There's also a second task starting for the mktemp command that handles basic template and file creation. I need to implement the mktemp command with requirements R1.1 through R1.4, creating both the main implementation and differential tests that compare against the reference gmktemp binary. I'll follow the project convention of calling the SIGPIPE handler at startup and use the testutils framework to validate behavior with LC_ALL=C set in the test environment.\n\nNow I'm looking at the acceptance criteria and the next phase of work, which covers suffix and directory mode functionality for requirements R1.5 and R2.1 through R2.3. I'm looking at the structure for implementing the mktemp command with support for R1.5 and R2.1-R2.3 requirements, modifying both the main implementation and test files to follow existing patterns and use differential testing against the gmktemp reference binary. Writing test specifications...\n\nI'm also noticing that the collision test fixtures exist as separate files, so I should call those out in the design decisions so the agent knows they're there. And I realize the requirement descriptions are pretty generic—I don't actually know what each R-item specifies without reading the SRD itself, which is why I'm including it in the required reading section. I should probably be more specific about what these requirements likely cover based on typical mktemp functionality, but I'll be honest that I need to reference the actual spec to fill in those details accurately. I'm verifying that my task structure maps each SRD R-item to exactly one requirement without splitting or merging unrelated items. Looking at the git history, I see ln work is already done through R4.2, so R4.3 is the next uncovered item, while mktemp hasn't been started yet. I should also make sure to reference the collision fixture context from CLAUDE.md so the stitch agent understands the mktemp setup requirements.\n\nSince both ln R4.3 and mktemp are part of rel06.0, and mktemp is the larger remaining piece with all requirements ready, I'll stick with covering those three mktemp tasks rather than branching into other rel06.1 items—rel06.0 is the earliest incomplete release and should be prioritized.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the line budget constraints. The ln R4.3 task is likely just a small modification under 50 lines, which falls short of the 300-500 target, but it's a single requirement with no other work to bundle with it. The mktemp tasks with 4 requirements each should fit the target range better, especially since the first one includes package scaffolding from scratch.\n\nLooking at typical cmd/ packages in this project, main.go usually runs 100-300 lines and tests add another 50-200, so a mktemp task with 4 features should land around 200-400 lines total—well within budget. I'm confident in this plan now.\n\nOne thing I need to verify: my design decisions like sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() and the RunDiffTests pattern both come from the architecture documentation, so they're grounded in the SRD and not invented.\n\nAlso, the cmd/mktemp/ directory already exists with collision fixture files but no Go source code yet, so the first task will create main.go in that existing directory. And since this is a cmd package (not a library), I don't need to propose a contract task first—the constraint about stubs applies to new packages with exported types and interfaces, which a main package doesn't have. with main.go and differential tests in each utility directory, plus shared testing infrastructure in pkg/testutils/. The project also has syscall abstractions for cross-platform support, formatting utilities, and specialized libraries for hashing, size parsing, and encoding. Build automation is handled through magefiles, and specifications live in docs/. We're currently on generation run 44 working toward rel06.0, which focuses on file operations—mkdir and rmdir are done, mktemp is ready to start with all requirements documented, and ln is mostly complete pending some R4.3 work.\n\nLooking at what needs attention next, rel06.0 is the earliest release with ready requirements. I need to prioritize finishing ln's remaining requirement and then tackle mktemp, which has 18 requirements all prepared but no implementation yet. With a 4-task budget, I'm planning one task to complete ln and three tasks to cover about two-thirds of mktemp's requirements, leaving the rest for the next batch.\n\nVerifying the weight distribution across the four tasks confirms everything fits within the budget, with each task carrying a total weight of 4 or less.\n\nNow I'm refining the task descriptions to ensure they're truly self-contained. For the ln R4.3 task, I should clarify that the utility is mostly done and this is just adding the final missing feature, so the stitch agent knows it's modifying existing work rather than building from scratch. For the mktemp tasks, I want to be explicit about whether each one is creating the initial implementation or modifying what came before, and I should call out the specific patterns to follow like the cmd/ package structure and sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(). The descriptions I have already cover these points, so I think I'm ready to finalize the YAML.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53052,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53052},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b45ed9e0-9270-4282-a9e7-2422d05d79ac","uuid":"18a1d3e8-abd4-4a80-8936-6479e25f7094"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012akrahdDz6tQ1PF1RgTFDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator) using Unix utilities as the test bed.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` holds one utility per directory (main.go + differential tests). `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness. `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls. `pkg/format/` handles output formatting. `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/`, `pkg/encutil/` provide shared utility libraries. `docs/` holds SRDs as the specification source of truth.\n\n**Current State**: 33 releases (00.0–15.0) covering 111 utilities. Many are implemented through previous generation runs. Generation run 44 is in progress on `generation-run44`.\n\n**Current Release**: rel06.0 (file/directory creation and removal). Within this release: mkdir (done), rmdir (done), unlink (done), ln (implemented but R4.3 remaining), mktemp (not started, all 18 SRD requirements ready).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe earliest release with ready requirements is **rel06.0**:\n1. **srd037-ln R4.3** — one remaining requirement for an already-implemented utility\n2. **srd036-mktemp** — 18 requirements all ready, code not started\n\nWith max 4 tasks: 1 for ln R4.3, 3 for mktemp (covers 12 of 18 requirements; remaining 6 for next batch).\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0: srd037-ln R4.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd036-mktemp R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd036-mktemp R1.5 (w=1), R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd036-mktemp R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1), R3.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\nAll within budget (assuming default weight 1; weights not verifiable without file access).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ln implementation -- version and help output (srd037-ln R4.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd037-ln.yaml (R4.3 requirement only)\n      - cmd/ln/main.go (existing implementation -- modify, do not rewrite)\n      - cmd/ln/ln_test.go (existing differential tests -- add new cases)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ln/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R4.3 functionality to existing implementation\n      - path: cmd/ln/ln_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R4.3 scenarios\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd037-ln R4.3 per the SRD specification\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the existing code structure and patterns in cmd/ln/main.go -- this is a modification, not a rewrite\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests to compare against gln reference binary\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Add new DiffTest entries to the existing tests slice in ln_test.go\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"R4.3 functionality implemented in cmd/ln/main.go\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential test cases added for R4.3 scenarios\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go build -o bin/ln ./cmd/ln/ succeeds\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/ln/ -count=1 passes\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/mktemp implementation -- basic template and file creation (srd036-mktemp R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd036-mktemp.yaml (R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - pkg/sys/sig